Help For The Split and Repeaters

l: Split/repeater. Outside FM, enter the transmit frequency in MHz; receive stays on the selected VFO and the other VFO receives the transmit frequency and a copy of the receive mode. This replaces the other VFO frequency/mode. In FM, enter a signed repeater offset in hertz, e.g. minus 600000, unless a band default exists in yac.ini. Blank or q cancels with Back; h then Enter repeats help. Press l again to turn existing split/repeater operation off. Native FM shift preserves tone/code settings. Defaults in [yac]: repeater_offset_10m_hz, repeater_offset_6m_hz, repeater_offset_2m_hz, repeater_offset_70cm_hz, repeater_offset_23cm_hz. No regional offsets are guessed or saved automatically; edit the INI to change defaults. Entered offsets are temporary but the radio menu value remains until changed. Readback confirms base RX/TX frequencies, not measured RF. Enabling requires readable VFO-mode state and inactive RIT/XIT/clarifiers. FTX-1 control target must match VS. IC-9700 uses MAIN A/B, not satellite mode. Yaesu FT-DX10/FT-710/FTX-1 and Icom IC-705/IC-7300/IC-7300MK2/IC-7600/IC-9700 profiles are provided; rejected or unavailable commands stop setup. Kenwood/QMX are not yet supported. q at the top level still quits. No transmitting test is started.

Consecutive w presses alternate normal status and live split/repeater details: receive frequency, transmit frequency and active FM tone/code. Off is announced; failed reads are unknown. Any other command resets the sequence.
For an offset of minus 600000 hertz, type a minus sign followed by 600000. For plus 600000 hertz, type 600000; a leading plus sign is optional. Status uses the words Plus or Minus before the offset value.
Restore Failed after split setup means YAC could not confirm restoration of every previous setting. Release the push-to-talk switch. At the main interface, consecutive w presses alternate normal status and live split/repeater details, including receive and transmit frequencies. Read these before transmitting; do not assume the previous settings were restored. If status cannot be read, resolve the radio connection first.

